title: Overview - Data Shape (v1.0)

''Reference for the data shape — look up entity fields here.'' For the narrative intro see [[Overview - Vocabularies & Markers (v1.0)]].

Four entities, three relationships. Everything is a tiddler; activation is materialised by a tag and a name — there is no separate registration table.

[img[cm-v1-data-shape.svg]]

!! The three relationships

; ''Source Tiddler'' → ''Vocabulary''  (activates)
: The author opts into a vocab's markers via the ''type field'' (`type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=A,B`) or an in-source ''pragma'' (`\importcustom [tag[vocab/X]]`). Both paths reach the same `registry.activate()`. With no `;vocab=`, `vocab/default` is implicit. Collision rule for shared `open` literals: last activated wins (see [[Overview - Vocabularies & Markers (v1.0)]] § Vocabulary collisions).

; ''Vocabulary'' → ''Marker''  (groups)
: A marker belongs to a vocabulary by carrying that vocabulary's title in its `tags`. There is no `marker-tag` field on the vocabulary (dropped in beta-35) — the relationship is pure tag-membership. ''Title convention:'' `vocab/<lowercase-caption>` lets `registry.activate(name)` do a direct `getTiddler` instead of a filter walk (~33× faster than the pre-beta-29 path).

; ''Marker'' → ''MarkerKind''  (kind)
: The `kind` field is the discriminator that decides which other fields are honoured. `close` only matters for `inline-pair`; `max-level` only for `glyph-level`; `container` / `item-element` / `indent-unit` only for `list-item`; `paragraph-marker` / `emit-open` / `end-string` for the block kinds. See [[Overview - Vocabularies & Markers (v1.0)]] § The five marker kinds for narrative + worked examples.

!! Vocabulary fields

|! Field |! Notes |
|`title` |Must be `vocab/<lowercase-caption>` for fast activation. |
|`tags` |Must include `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary`. |
|`caption` · `description` |Human-readable. |
|`disable-core-rules`? |Whitespace-separated TW core wikirule names to remove when this vocab activates. Applied via `parser.amendRules("except", ...)` for the active tiddler only. Lets Markdown claim `_`, `~~`, `|`; lets Fountain claim `!`, `#`. |
|`front-matter`? |`yes` → consume a YAML block at parser position 0. |

!! Marker fields

Clustered by job. Most markers only need a few fields from the first two clusters.

; identity
: `title` (convention `vocab/<v>/<NAME>`)  ·  `tags` (`$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker` + `vocab/<v>`)  ·  `caption`  ·  `description`

; matching
: `kind`  ·  `open`  ·  `close` (inline-pair)  ·  `open-pattern` (list-item, overrides `open`)  ·  `max-level` (glyph-level, default 4)  ·  `allow-symbol` (glyph, inline-pair)

; output
: `element` (html-tag or `$widget`; default `div` for block / `span` for inline-pair)  ·  `classes` (dot-prefixed chain, e.g. `.a.b.c`)  ·  `attributes` (JSON)  ·  `container` / `item-element` / `indent-unit` (list-item)

; body parsing
: `mode` (`block` or `inline`)  ·  `paragraph-marker` (blank-line terminator)  ·  `end-string` (custom close)  ·  `emit-open` (keep the keyword in output)  ·  `body-raw` (inline-pair: literal text node)  ·  `src-name` (widget elements: rename the body attribute)

; editor &amp; back-compat
: `marker-icon`  ·  `order` (toolbar sort)  ·  `legacy-kind` (v0.x pragma bridge)  ·  `allow-classes` (word: append `.cls` after keyword)  ·  `debug` / `debug-string`

; security
: `allow-unsafe` (default `no`: iframe gets `sandbox=""`, `object`/`embed`/`frame` denied, `javascript:` URLs stripped). See [[Custom Markup Security]] for the full threat model.

!! Two side channels not on the diagram

* ''Global Pragma tiddlers'' (tagged `$:/tags/Pragma`) reach every parser through `$:/config/custom-markup/pragma/PageTemplate`, which simply contains `\importcustom [tag[$:/tags/Pragma]]`. Parsed pragmas are cached per wiki (~3× speedup).
* ''HTML output'' from a fired marker: `element` (from marker) + classes `wltc` + `wltc-l<N>` (glyph-level only) + `marker.classes`, with attributes scrubbed per the security rules above.

!! Example marker tiddler

Fountain's scene-heading marker. Three required fields plus three opt-ins:

```
title:   vocab/fountain/INT
tags:    $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker  [[vocab/fountain]]
caption: Int.
kind:    word
open:    INT.
element: p
classes: .wltc-fountain-scene-heading
mode:    inline
emit-open: yes
paragraph-marker: yes
```

